// DotProductSgn -- the Pyrope equivalent of verilog/DotProductSgn.sv (DatapathBench).
//
// Hand-written, not emitted from the Verilog: a machine emission would enter
// the same LGraph the Verilog does and measure the two FRONT ENDS rather than
// the two languages. See [status].pyrope in design.toml.
//
// Ports keep the Verilog names and the widths of the pinned point (BW = 10),
// so the generated harness and LEC bind the same external interface.
//
// Two-term signed dot product, truncated to the 20-bit result.
pub comb DotProductSgn(a:s10, b:s10, c:s10, d:s10) -> (res:s20) { wrap  res = (a*b) + (c*d) }
